                    {
                        "sense_id": "84981f2d-046a-326b-9f88-b0985df106c4",
                        "entry_id": "5b4265f9-8f5b-3ef7-a58d-74e7544137e8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That sustains, supports or provides sustenance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e51bce38-50d9-4bb6-b44a-d5b59b7b419c",
                                "sense_id": "84981f2d-046a-326b-9f88-b0985df106c4",
                                "text": "[…] eternall life, the end of all our wearisome labours, and all our sustaining hopes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1433a727-a1df-4bfd-b15f-550bcb87e362",
                                "sense_id": "84981f2d-046a-326b-9f88-b0985df106c4",
                                "text": "1771, Elizabeth Griffith, The History of Lady Barton, London: T. Davies & T. Cadell, Volume 2, Letter 31, p. 21,\nI turned quick to look for him, and saw him coming towards me, with another gentleman—But I saw no more, my senses forsook me; in spite of Maria’s sustaining arm, I fell motionless on the ground."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60eb84ae-104d-4c1a-828c-43384895b672",
                                "sense_id": "84981f2d-046a-326b-9f88-b0985df106c4",
                                "text": "Sometimes, I had proceeded restlessly from place to place, stopping nowhere; sometimes, I had lingered long in one spot. I had had no purpose, no sustaining soul within me, anywhere."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "523233c4-6f45-428b-8b5d-4ad3f91bc157",
                                "sense_id": "84981f2d-046a-326b-9f88-b0985df106c4",
                                "text": "They laughed and chattered, and passed each other sustaining bits of chocolate in torn silver paper."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d5b7013-1ddf-428a-bd20-2cec14687109",
                                "sense_id": "84981f2d-046a-326b-9f88-b0985df106c4",
                                "text": "[…] I was thirsty & went to sit in the shade of the tea-terrace. The tea, served impractically in a glass, was refreshing, somehow muddy & more sustaining than tea I am used to."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
